Experiment 4.1: Middle of Linked List (Leetcode Problem-876)
Aim: To find the middle node of a singly linked list using the slow and fast pointer technique.

Algorithm:
1. Initialize two pointers slow and fast at the head.
2. Move slow one step at a time.
3. Move fast two steps at a time.
4. Continue until fast reaches the end of the list.
5. When the loop ends, slow points to the middle node.
6. Return slow.

Code:
class Solution {
public:
    ListNode* middleNode(ListNode* head) {
        ListNode* slow = head;
    ListNode* fast = head;

    while (fast != NULL && fast->next != NULL) {
        slow = slow->next;
        fast = fast->next->next;
    }

    return slow;
    }
};


Experiment 4.2: Palindrome Linked List (Leetcode Problem-234)
Aim: To check whether a singly linked list is a palindrome by comparing its elements from the beginning and end.

Algorithm:
1. Initialize an empty stack st.
2. Traverse the linked list and push every node's value into the stack.
3. Traverse the linked list again from the head.
4. Compare each node's value with the top value of the stack.
5. If any values are different, return false.
6. Pop the top element after each comparison.
7. If all values match, return true.

Code:
class Solution {
public:
    bool isPalindrome(ListNode* head) {

        stack<int> st;
        ListNode* temp = head;

        // Put all values into stack
        while (temp != NULL) {
            st.push(temp->val);
            temp = temp->next;
        }

        // Compare linked list with stack
        temp = head;

        while (temp != NULL) {

            if (temp->val != st.top()) {
                return false;
            }

            st.pop();
            temp = temp->next;
        }

        return true;
    }
};
